# Problem Statement

![Problem 8.2](../imgs/gelfand-fomin_8_2.png)

# Solution

## Exact Solution

![Problem 8.2](../imgs/exact_soln_8_2.png)

We will define the julia function of this for comparison against the approximations
```julia; results="hidden"
y_exact(x) = sin(x) / sin(1) - x
have_exact = !isnothing(y_exact)
```

## Ritz Approximations
We will use the `RitzMethod` package
```julia; results="hidden"
using RitzMethod
import Optim
import Plots

# Define problem and basis
integrand(x, y, y_prime) = y_prime^2 - y^2 - 2 * x * y
domain = Interval(0.0, 1.0)
full_basis = [x -> x^k * (1 - x) for k in 1:3]

function solve_ritz(n_terms)
    minimizefunctional(
        integrand, domain, full_basis[1:n_terms];
        num_quad_nodes=5,
        method=Optim.BFGS(),
        options=Optim.Options(iterations=50, g_abstol=1e-20, x_reltol=1e-8),
    )
end

results = [solve_ritz(n) for n in 1:3]
```

### One-Term Approximation

```julia;
println(summarize(results[1]))
```

### Two-Term Approximation

```julia;
println(summarize(results[2]))
```

### Three-Term Approximation

```julia;
println(summarize(results[3]))
```

# Comparison

```julia; echo=false
using Printf
println("Term count | Minimized J[y] | Coefficients")
for (n, r) in enumerate(results)
    @printf("%-10d | %-14.8f | %s\n", n, r.minimized_value, r.coeffs)
end
```

```julia; echo=false; fig_cap="Ritz Approximations"
xs = range(domain.low, domain.high; length=200)
plt = Plots.plot(xs, results[1].y.(xs); label="1-term", xlabel="x", ylabel="y(x)")
Plots.plot!(plt, xs, results[2].y.(xs); label="2-term")
Plots.plot!(plt, xs, results[3].y.(xs); label="3-term")
if have_exact
    Plots.plot!(plt, xs, y_exact.(xs); label="exact", linestyle=:dash, linewidth=2)
end
plt
```

# Approximation Error

```julia; echo=false; fig_cap="Pointwise error between Ritz approximations and the exact solution."
if have_exact
    err_plt = Plots.plot(xs, results[1].y.(xs) .- y_exact.(xs); label="1-term", xlabel="x", ylabel="Absolute Error")
    Plots.plot!(err_plt, xs, results[2].y.(xs) .- y_exact.(xs); label="2-term")
    Plots.plot!(err_plt, xs, results[3].y.(xs) .- y_exact.(xs); label="3-term")
    err_plt
end
```
